  "provider_query": "CPython source file that defines PyObject_Malloc",
  "answer": "**`PyObject_Malloc` is defined in `Objects/obmalloc.c`.**\n\nRelevant CPython locations:\n\n1. **`Objects/obmalloc.c`** — definition of `PyObject_Malloc(size_t size)`; checks size against `PY_SSIZE_T_MAX`, updates allocation stats, then calls `_PyObject.malloc`. Also holds related allocators (`_PyObject_Malloc`, mimalloc paths).  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Objects/obmalloc.c\n\n2. **`Include/objimpl.h`** — public declaration: `PyAPI_FUNC(void *) PyObject_Malloc(size_t size);` with notes on the object allocator.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/objimpl.h\n\n3. **`Doc/c-api/memory.rst`** — C API docs: allocates *n* bytes, zero-byte request behavior, GIL/thread-state requirement, pymalloc vs mimalloc defaults.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/memory.rst\n\n4. **`Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h`** — internal pymalloc/object-allocator overview (layer used by `PyObject_Malloc` / object allocation).  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h\n\n5. **`Include/internal/pycore_object_alloc.h`** — `_PyObject_MallocWithType` and heap selection (including free-threaded/mimalloc) that call `PyObject_Malloc`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Include/internal/pycore_object_alloc.h\n\n6. **`Doc/c-api/allocation.rst`** — higher-level object macros (`PyObject_New`, etc.) that allocate via `PyObject_Malloc`; deprecated aliases such as `PyObject_MALLOC`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/allocation.rst\n\n7. **PR #23587** — replaced deprecated `PyObject_MALLOC()` aliases with `PyObject_Malloc()` (bpo-42519).  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/23587\n\n8. **PR #4199** — added documentation for `PyObject_Malloc`, `PyObject_Calloc`, `PyObject_Realloc`, and `PyObject_Free` (bpo-20064).  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/4199",
